<title>INDIA: India's TELCO 1996/97 net seen higher.</title>
<headline>India's TELCO 1996/97 net seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's biggest truck maker Tata Engineering and Locomotive Company Ltd (TELCO) is projected to push its net profit 28.68 percent higher to 6.82 billion rupees in the year ended March 31, 1997, a Reuter poll showed.</p>
<p>Analysts at 28 leading securities and brokerage firms forecast a low of 6.37 billion rupees and a high of 7.20 billion rupees against 5.30 billion in the year ago period.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>TELCO   ----PAT seen up 28.68%, sales up 16.92%</p>
<p>			Net profit  1995/96     Net sales  1995/96</p>
<p>				 (in million rupees)</p>
<p>Average		6,819.78  5,300.00    91,966.79  78,657.00</p>
<p>High		   7,205.00		 104,900.00</p>
<p>Low		    6,371.00		  81,978.00</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
